[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708676049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103843#issuecomment-2708676049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103843","id":2708676049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hcx3R","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T05:11:41Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T05:11:41Z","body":"The problem is that `@tool` is applied to the **script**, not the **class**. All classes located in the tool script are marked as tool classes. So when you inherit an inner class from a tool script, you get the warning, even if you didn't mean for the inner class to be a tool.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708676049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708684946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103843#issuecomment-2708684946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103843","id":2708684946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hc0CS","user":{"login":"EmilyV99","id":35015090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDE1MDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35015090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99","html_url":"https://github.com/EmilyV99","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EmilyV99/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T05:49:02Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T05:49:02Z","body":"That makes some sense, and I would not have questioned it, if not for the fact that it did not give these warnings in 4.3, which seemed like an odd change- though as long as this change was an intentional expansion of the warning, it seems sensible enough.\n\nIt also does NOT propagate through multiple inheritances- ex. if I have `TestA extends ToolScript.Something` and `TestB extends TestA`, only the definition of `TestA` fires the warning, which seems odd- though I'm unsure how that works with normal tool scripts either.\n\nI would then question if there could be some way to mark a class as not tool, though `@warning_ignore(\"missing_tool\")` is simple enough to add I suppose? Though that needs to be added at every extending location, so an annotation on the defining location might be nice","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708684946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708757337","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103843#issuecomment-2708757337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103843","id":2708757337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hdFtZ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T09:30:31Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T09:30:31Z","body":"> I would then question if there could be some way to mark a class as not tool, though `@warning_ignore(\"missing_tool\")` is simple enough to add I suppose?\n\nI think the warning is correct, since currently inner classes in tool scripts are also tool classes. If you inherit from an inner class and get the warning, it helps you think about why this is happening. You can have unexpected bugs because the base inner class is in tool mode and its inheritors are not.\n\nWe can't change the current behavior for compatibility reasons, but in theory we could introduce a `@no_tool` annotation so you could have non-tool inner classes inside a tool outer class. For now, you can move the inner classes out of the tool script or use `@warning_ignore(\"missing_tool\")` if you are sure everything works as you want.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708757337/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]